<h1>Scan Pane (Arm Menu)</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="Description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Scan Pane is one of the three panes located in the left hand side of the KUBE window. All these panes are overlapped and can be switched between by clicking on their tabs (which are in the lower left hand side) or by shortcuts (<span class="Shortcut">Ctrl + 1</span> for Scan pane).</p>
<table cellspacing="5" width="801" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/scan_pane.jpg" width="233px" height="427px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="middle" class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">The KUBE software Scan Menu is designed to be operated by moving the localiser up and down. If &#160;the localiser has not been previously used with KUBE, the direction of movement will need to be calibrated. To do this, select</span> <span class="Path"><a href="localiser_menu_operation.htm">System &gt; Localiser Menu Operation &gt; Calibrate</a></span> <span lang="EN-GB">and follow the on-screen wizard.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">The up/down movement of the localiser can be used to highlight different menu items. The menus are operated via the switches Left</span> <span lang="EN-GB">('A') button and Right ('B') button.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">If the commands from this menu cannot fit, scrolling buttons appear so that if you reach some of them by the localiser or press with the mouse the Scan pane will scroll up or down.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/scroll_localiser_menu.gif" width="218px" height="137px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="normal-table">The 'Scan Pane' is divided in two parts:</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Description">Localiser Menu (Scan buttons)</a></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Description1">Display windows for probe and sensor</a></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="#Voice">Voice and laser control buttons</a></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="normal-table">The buttons from the three sub-menus (Single-site, Multi-site, and Datum) of 'Scan Pane' can be added, removed, and rearranged. See <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Arm Menu Appearance &gt;</b></i></span> <a href="../References/Preferences_-_Arm_Menu_Appearance_-_Scan.htm">Scan</a>, <a href="../References/Preferences_-_Arm_Menu_Appearance_-_Multi-site.htm">Multi-site</a>, and <a href="../References/Preferences_-_Arm_Menu_Appearance_-_Datum.htm">Datum</a>, for details about customisation of these menus.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Description"></a>Description of Scan Buttons</p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="803" class="whs10">
<col class="whs11">
<col class="whs12">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="20.926%" class="whs13">
<p class="caption">Button</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="78.995%" class="whs14">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="20.926%" class="whs15">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/PreScan.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
<td width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> PreScan is used to position and orientate the localiser, to find the optimum position for KUBE and the scanned object. PreScan will either add data to the current document (keeping all existing entities) or open a new document, depending on the selection with the on-screen wizard. To assist with visualisation, PreScan displays a bounding box of the complete XYZ range of data captured. If PreScan is not used, &#160;no scan data will appear on screen.</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Choose PreScan from the KUBE options, by raising or lowering the localiser until the option is highlighted. Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to select.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Do a rough scan of the object, acquiring data until full coverage is obtained, (i.e. enough points are captured on screen).</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to end PreScan.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Warning" id="P1">The data acquired in PreScan is not used in the actual scanning of the object. It is only used as a guide to obtaining the ideal position of the object.</p>
<p id="P2" class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> If the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Enter scan mode immediately after prescan/autoset mode</b></span>' option (in <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings / Scan Mode</b></span> dialog) is enabled you directly enter Scan mode (in pause) when exit PreScan.</p>
<p id="P1">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="20.926%" class="whs15">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/Scan.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
<td width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Scan generates data in the form of points from the object being scanned.</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Choose Scan from the KUBE options, by raising or lowering the localiser until the option is highlighted. Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to select.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">KUBE is automatically in 'Pause' mode. The '<span class="Mode">Pause'</span> mode is represented on the PC display as a '<span class="Button">Pause'</span> button.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>If Sensor Model option is enabled the current model of the sensor/localiser is dynamically displayed on the screen. See <a href="../References/Preferences_-_Display_-_Sensor_Models.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Sensor Model</a> for details.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a22" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for MM Z with FARO/ComCore</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP169093579" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/SensorModel_MMZ.gif" width="394px" height="304px" border="0" class="img_whs18" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for MM D with FARO/CimCore</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP171902290" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/SensorModel_MMD.gif" width="394px" height="304px" border="0" class="img_whs18" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for MM C with FARO/CimCore</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP172318179" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/SensorModel_MMC.gif" width="394px" height="304px" border="0" class="img_whs18" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for MM Z with K-Scan</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP168731724" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/SensorModel_KScan.gif" width="394px" height="304px" border="0" class="img_whs18" alt=""></p>
</div>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Press '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' button to select 'Scan' mode. (Using the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' button toggle, ModelMaker can be repositioned between passes at the object.)</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Move scanner around the object and acquire data until happy with results.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to finish the scan.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>When in '<span class="Mode">Pause'</span> mode the following actions are available:</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Hold the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' button to temporary enter '<span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>View</u></span>' mode. This option and its behaviour is controlled from in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings / Scan Mode</b></i></span> dialog (Immediate View during Pause).</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Hold the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'A'</b></span> button to delete the last scanned patch. This option is controlled from in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings / Scan Mode</b></i></span> dialog (Remove last patch).</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Quickly depress the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'B'</b></span> button twice (equivalent to double-click the mouse button) to switch between Normal and Fast Scan mode. This option is controlled from in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings / Scan Mode</b></i></span> dialog (Activate fast scanning via trigger button). It is applicable to ModelMaker D sensors only.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>During scanning info about number of scanned points and memory usage is shown in the status bar.</p>
<p><img src="../images/status.gif" width="929px" height="28px" border="0" class="img_whs19" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="20.926%" class="whs15">
<p class="normal-table"><a name="Autoset_Laser_power"></a><img src="../images/autoset_laser.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Autoset Laser determines the proper laser power level for scanning different surfaces (dark, light, shiny, etc.).</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Choose Autoset Laser from the KUBE options, by raising or lowering the localiser until the option is highlighted. Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to select.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Point the sensor somewhere to the object surface.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' button to start. Hold the sensor still during detection.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">When done, press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' button to set the new laser power level.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> If there is some data loaded / scanned and the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Enter scan mode immediately after prescan/autoset mode</b></span>' option (in <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings / Scan Mode</b></span> dialog) is enabled, then when Autoset Laser command is completed you directly enter Scan mode (in pause).</p>
<p class="Bullet">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="20.926%" class="whs15">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/view.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
<td width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> View displays the data acquired in Scan from the current location of the sensor. Used to position the sensor to the optimum scanning position.</p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Choose 'View' from the KUBE options, by raising or lowering the localiser until the option is highlighted. Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button too select.</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Move the sensor, and the data of the object will be presented on the PC, viewed from the current location of the sensor.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle">To Zoom In - move the sensor closer to the object</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle">To Zoom Out - move the sensor further away from the object</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle">To Pan - move the sensor left/right/up/down</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-circle">
<p class="bullet-circle">To Rotate the view - rotate the sensor</p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Press the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to exit this mode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P4"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> After exit <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>'View'</u></span> mode the Scan button is automatically highlighted (but KUBE does not enter Scan mode.)</p>
<p class="Bullet">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
