<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="20.926%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/save.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Save allows the scan data to be saved while scanning.</p>
<p>If it is new scan data, the file will be saved in the KUBE installation directory under the name "KubeSave.sab2". If a file with the same exist, KUBE will prompt to replace the file.</p>
<p>If the file has already been saved, it will be saved now under its original name.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="20.926%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/profiles.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p>User can select predefined profiles from the menu by using the localiser. <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Hardware Settings</b></span> allows the user to configure ModelMaker once for a certain type of object and save those settings for future use. For example, when scanning black leather the laser power is likely to be higher than scanning grey fabric. More details about using profiles<a href="../Scanning/Scanning/profiles.htm" target="_self"><img src="../images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></a>.</p>
<p class="Note" id="P5"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> After exit Profiles command the Scan button is automatically highlighted (but KUBE does not enter Scan mode.)</p>
<p class="Bullet">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="20.926%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/stand_by.jpg" width="120px" height="30px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td width="78.995%" class="whs17">
<p>This button is not visible by default. It can be added to the displayed arm buttons via <a href="../References/Preferences_-_Arm_Menu_Appearance_-_Scan.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt;Arm Menu Appearance &gt;Scan</a>. Any button operation in this position is ignored. This is a safety feature to protect any recent scan data from accidental modification. The localiser will automatically select this item when in a standby position.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="whs36">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">&#160;<a name="Description1"></a>Description of view windows in the Scan Pane</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><a href="../References/display_localiser_position.htm">Display Arm Position</a></b></span> window shows the current localiser probe co-ordinates according to the global co-ordinate system. This window is hidden by default.</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><a href="../References/display_sensor.htm">Display Sensor</a></b></span> displays the laser stripe in red colour when the '<span class="Button">Laser'</span> button is on. This window is hidden by default.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head"><a name="Voice"></a>Laser Voice control buttons</p>
<table cellspacing="0" width="804" class="whs37">
<col class="whs38">
<col class="whs39">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="25.855%" class="whs40">
<p class="caption">Button</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="74.145%" class="whs41">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="25.855%" class="whs42">
<p class="normal-table-func"><img src="../images/laser.gif" width="164px" height="20px" border="0" class="img_whs43" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Button">Laser On/Off Button</span></p>
</td>
<td width="74.145%" class="whs44">
<p class="normal-table">Click on it to activate or deactivate the laser. This button is always visible.</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="25.855%" class="whs45">
<p class="normal-table-func"><img src="../images/voice.gif" width="164px" height="19px" border="0" class="img_whs46" alt=""></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Button">Voice On/Off</span> Button</p>
</td>
<td width="74.145%" class="whs44">
<p class="normal-table">Click on it to activate or deactivate the voice control i.e. to operate the sensor using your voice. The keywords and commands available are all those words found in the Scan menu e.g. 'PreScan', 'Scan' etc. During <span class="Mode">Scan</span> mode, press 'Start' to start scanning and 'Stop' to pause. This button is hidden by default. Its visibility is controlled by a checkbox in <a href="../References/Preferences_-_Audio.htm" target="_self">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Audio</a> dialog.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>

